       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, and kidney and liver function don't change that.\n\nThe dose may have been a typo or a mix-up between per-dose and daily totals. These are some possible intended orders:\n\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 1,700 mg/day total.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** These are common regimens.\n\nPlease tell me which dose you want. If 1700 mg three times daily is what you meant, tell me that and any note you want on the order, such as the clinical rationale. I'll then enter it as you specify."
      }
