       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still haven't entered the order. As far as I know, the current FDA label doesn't allow this dose. For adults, the label sets these maximums:\n\n- **Immediate-release:** 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily.\n- **Extended-release:** 2,000 mg/day.\n\nThe order as written is 5,100 mg/day, about twice the immediate-release maximum. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual single-dose ceiling of 850 to 1,000 mg. If you're looking at a source that says otherwise, please check it again. It may be listing a different figure, such as a total daily dose.\n\nI can enter either of these now:\n\n1. **A label-compliant order**, such as 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day).\n2. **The order as written (1700 mg PO TID), as a deliberate above-label dose.** For this I'd need you to say you know it exceeds the labeled maximum. I'd also add a note with the clinical rationale so pharmacy and nursing can see it's intentional.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
